{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Explains the policy purpose; does not independently impose an approval condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u0.2"},{"reason":"Establishes the UCITS post-authorisation setting and immediate-effect description, read with the express Effective Date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u1.190"},{"reason":"Heading identifying the subject of the measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u2.523"},{"reason":"Limits the enumerated measures to post-authorisation matters.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"reason":"Separate operator-change measure; its express supervision condition is not automatically imported into the investment-change rule.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u4.653"},{"reason":"Provides the home-requirements condition and product-feature and local-policy exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"reason":"Separate notification measure; approval relief does not establish that notification is unnecessary.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"},{"reason":"Identifies FAQs, forms and checklists whose substantive contents are absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u7.1419"},{"reason":"Implementation heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u8.1677"},{"reason":"Fixes the Effective Date at 28 November 2025.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"reason":"Preserves existing processing for pending applications received before the Effective Date; the precise substantive consequences remain unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"reason":"Identifies management companies as the audience of the following oversight passage.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},{"reason":"Preserves post-vetting and possible regulatory follow-up despite prior-approval relief.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},{"reason":"Provides a clarification route without adding a substantive approval condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},{"reason":"Signatory division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing body.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},{"reason":"Defines the covered UCITS population by domicile and status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"reason":"FAQ reference only; linked substantive requirements cannot be determined from this packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},{"reason":"Forms and checklists reference only; linked contents cannot be determined from this packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control concerns material investment changes in the post-authorisation setting for the circular's defined UCITS funds. Management companies are addressed, but the relief attaches to scheme changes. Other funds and operator changes are outside this selected control.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u11.2030","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"UCITS funds is expressly defined. Materiality, novel or complex product features, home-jurisdiction compliance and possible local policy implications lack operational definitions in the supplied text.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The exceptions attach to approval relief for investment changes: novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications independently defeats the stated relief. The language does not support requiring all three together.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The text removes a prior-approval requirement for qualifying changes. It does not certify compliance or eliminate notification, filing, post-vetting or regulatory action. Failure to qualify for removal does not itself fully establish the underlying approval obligation.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The express date is 28 November 2025. Pre-date applications pending at transition retain existing processing. Whether this necessarily preserves a substantive prior-approval prerequisite, rather than just the handling of the application, is not fully specified.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The operative FAQs, referenced forms and checklists, home requirements and existing approval process are not supplied. The two dependency records have no source hashes or contents, and cannot be reliably mapped to particular referenced documents.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What do the operative FAQs say about materiality, novelty, complexity and possible local policy implications?","Does retaining the existing approval process for a pending pre-Effective-Date application also preserve the substantive prerequisite of approval before implementation, and may the application be withdrawn to use the new measures?","Do the FAQs impose any separate home-supervision condition beyond compliance with home-jurisdiction requirements for investment changes?","What underlying approval rules apply where this circular's removal does not apply?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The express Effective Date supplies the date intended by the introductory immediate-effect language.","The selected formal control excludes applications caught by the transition, because their treatment requires the existing process and missing FAQs.","The introductory reference to home supervision describes the measures' purpose; it is not treated as an additional independently specified condition in item (ii)."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"The text supports a clear removal-of-approval eligibility rule for changes outside the transition, rather than rival conjunctive and disjunctive exception rules. For example, an ordinary home-compliant investment-policy change in a covered Irish UCITS after the Effective Date qualifies if it has no possible local policy implications; the same change with possible local policy implications does not qualify even if it is neither novel nor complex. For an otherwise identical application received on 27 November 2025 and pending at transition, existing processing applies and this formal control gives no answer. The strongest uncertainty is whether that preserved processing also necessarily preserves the substantive approval prerequisite.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS, within the circular's definition.","name":"covered_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change is a post-authorisation material change to the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"covered_material_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The date as of which availability of the circular's approval removal is assessed; this does not select an implementation-date test for every transitional situation.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"An application concerning this change was received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 and remained without approval or authorisation at the Effective Date.","name":"pending_legacy_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed investment change complies with the fund's applicable home-jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves novel product features.","name":"novel_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves complex product features.","name":"complex_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required by this wording.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and home_requirements_met (not (or novel_features complex_features possible_local_policy_implications)))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_ucits covered_material_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) (not pending_legacy_application))"},"local_id":"approval_removal_eligibility","questions":["For a pending legacy application, does existing processing require approval before the change can take effect, or only govern disposition of the already-filed application?","What evidence and interpretive standards establish home compliance and the absence of each exception under the missing FAQs?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for a material UCITS investment change outside the legacy-application transition. Within the stated scope, true means the change meets the circular's stated home-compliance condition and none of its stated exceptions applies. False means this removal is unavailable under those conditions; it does not independently establish a prohibition, non-compliance or the complete underlying approval obligation. Outside scope, the result supplies no determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.","subject":"Prior-approval removal for material changes to UCITS investment objectives, policies or restrictions"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Purpose informs interpretation but supplies no independent approval test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u0.2"},{"reason":"Identifies post-authorisation scope, home-supervision rationale and immediate-effect language.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u1.190"},{"reason":"Heading identifies the measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u2.523"},{"reason":"Limits the listed measures to post-authorisation matters.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"reason":"Separate operator-change measure; its express home-supervision condition is not automatically added to the investment-change test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u4.653"},{"reason":"Principal removal of prior approval, home-compliance condition and product/policy exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"reason":"Separate notification measure; removal of prior approval does not establish exemption from notification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"},{"reason":"Identifies implementation materials whose substantive contents are absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u7.1419"},{"reason":"Heading identifies implementation provisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u8.1677"},{"reason":"Supplies the express effective date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"reason":"Preserves existing processing for applications received before the effective date and still unapproved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"reason":"Identifies management companies as the audience for the following continuing oversight discussion; supplies no separate approval condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},{"reason":"Preserves post-vetting, discretionary enquiries and regulatory action despite removal of prior approval.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},{"reason":"Offers case-officer clarification without creating an approval test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},{"reason":"Issuer division attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},{"reason":"Issuer attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},{"reason":"Defines the eligible fund population exhaustively for this circular.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"reason":"FAQ reference is identified, but the linked substantive requirements are unavailable in the packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},{"reason":"Forms and checklists reference is identified, but the linked contents are unavailable in the packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"Selected control concerns material investment changes after authorisation for the specifically defined UCITS population. Operator changes and notifications are separate measures.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"UCITS population is expressly defined. Materiality, novelty, complexity and possible local policy implications require judgment; the packet supplies no operational thresholds.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The exception attaches to removal of prior approval. Novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications each defeat eligibility; home-jurisdiction compliance remains a separate necessary condition.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The measure removes an existing prior-approval requirement for qualifying changes. Excluded cases receive no removal under this limb; determining their actual approval obligation also requires the underlying regime. Post-vetting continues and follow-up action is discretionary.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"Use the express 28 November 2025 effective date to give content to immediate effect. The proposed reading treats pre-date applications still unapproved at that date as retained in the existing process. Whether that retention preserves every substantive approval condition remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Relevant FAQs implement the measures, and related forms/checklists are referenced but absent. The two missing dependency identifiers have no supplied substantive content or mapping sufficient to resolve these gaps.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Do the relevant FAQs define material changes, novel or complex product features, or changes that may have local policy implications?","Does retention of the existing process for pending applications preserve the substantive prior-approval requirement, or only the processing route?","What underlying approval provisions apply when a change fails the home-compliance condition or falls within a product/policy exception?","Does the home-supervision rationale impose an additional condition beyond compliance with home-jurisdiction requirements in item (ii)?","Can the substantive contents and mapping of missing.1c25ffdf5c1e10e0297748d5 and missing.79fb54125bb1f35a1d457fad be supplied?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The express effective date governs the general statement that the measures take immediate effect.","Whether an existing application remains unapproved is assessed at the effective date.","For this proposal, retention in the existing approval process excludes the pending application from the new removal of prior approval.","The stated home-supervision rationale does not add a distinct approval or supervision test to item (ii)'s express home-jurisdiction compliance condition.","The absent FAQs may qualify implementation; this is a reading of the supplied text only."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"This reading tests eligibility for the selected removal of prior approval. The strongest unresolved alternative concerns pending applications: 'existing ... process' could retain only procedure while permitting the new substantive relaxation. That alternative would change the outcome for an otherwise qualifying pre-date pending application, but the packet does not establish it sufficiently to select a second executable rule. Failure of this eligibility test alone does not prove that approval is legally required.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"defined_ucits_fund","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is a post-authorisation matter for the fund.","name":"post_authorisation_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is material and concerns the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"material_investment_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"Date as of which availability of the selected removal of prior approval is assessed.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The selected change complies with the fund's applicable home-jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change involves novel product features.","name":"novel_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change involves complex product features.","name":"complex_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change may have local policy implications; this asks about possibility, not only established actual effects.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"An application concerning the selected change was received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 and had received neither approval nor authorisation by that date.","name":"pending_pre_effective_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) home_requirements_met (not (or novel_features complex_features possible_local_policy_implications)) (not pending_pre_effective_application))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and defined_ucits_fund post_authorisation_change material_investment_change)"},"local_id":"removal_eligibility","questions":["Does the transition preserve substantive approval requirements as assumed, or only administrative processing?","What further qualifications do the referenced FAQs place on the selected removal?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the selected material investment change qualifies for removal of SFC prior approval under item (ii), on the proposed transition reading: the assessment is on or after 28 November 2025, home requirements are met, no novel or complex product features or possible local policy implications are involved, and no pre-effective pending application retains the existing process. False means this particular removal is unavailable under this reading; it does not independently establish an approval obligation or non-compliance. Unknown inputs remain unknown. Continuing notification and post-vetting obligations are outside this predicate.","subject":"Eligibility of a selected material UCITS investment change for removal of SFC prior approval"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Purpose and investor-protection context; creates no separate approval test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u0.2"},{"reason":"Establishes UCITS post-authorisation scope, home-supervision context and immediate-effect language.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u1.190"},{"reason":"Heading identifying the subject of the measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u2.523"},{"reason":"Limits the listed measures to post-authorisation matters.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"reason":"Separate operator-change measure; its express supervision condition is not automatically imported into the investment-change test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u4.653"},{"reason":"Supplies the selected approval-relief rule, home-requirements condition and product/local-policy exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"reason":"Separate notification measure; approval relief does not establish satisfaction of notice requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"},{"reason":"Identifies operative supporting FAQs, forms and checklists absent from the packet.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u7.1419"},{"reason":"Implementation heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u8.1677"},{"reason":"Supplies the express effective date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"reason":"Preserves existing processing for qualifying pending applications.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"reason":"Management-company heading; does not itself specify an additional duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},{"reason":"Preserves post-vetting and possible enquiries or regulatory action despite prior-approval relief.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},{"reason":"Provides a clarification channel, without defining the substantive test.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},{"reason":"Issuing-division identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},{"reason":"Issuer identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},{"reason":"Defines the geographically restricted UCITS population for this circular.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"reason":"FAQ reference identified; linked contents are unavailable and their interpretation is deferred.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},{"reason":"Forms/checklists reference identified; linked contents are unavailable and their interpretation is deferred.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control concerns material investment changes to already authorised funds within the circular's UCITS definition. Management companies are the operational audience; the SFC is the approving and post-vetting authority. The operator-change and notification measures are separate.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u4.653","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u11.2030","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"UCITS is expressly limited to the four named EU domiciles and UK-domiciled schemes authorised as UK UCITS. Materiality, novel or complex features, home requirements and potential local policy implications are not defined in the supplied text.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The exception attaches to removal of prior approval. Novel features, complex features or possible local policy implications each suffice to withhold that relief. Home-requirements compliance is a prerequisite. Failure of either test does not independently establish the underlying approval duty from this packet.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The operative measure removes a prior-approval requirement for qualifying changes. It does not approve the change, excuse home-law compliance or remove post-vetting. Post-vetting is stated to continue; follow-up enquiries and regulatory actions are discretionary possibilities.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The express date is 28 November 2025. The proposal reads 'immediate effect' consistently with that date, although the packet supplies no circular issue date. Pre-effective-date applications remaining unapproved follow the existing process; the precise assessment time for their pending status is unstated.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Implementation is expressly located in relevant FAQs. Those contents, related forms/checklists, applicable home requirements and the existing approval process are unavailable. Dependency identifiers missing.1c25ffdf5c1e10e0297748d5 and missing.79fb54125bb1f35a1d457fad have no supplied contents or explicit mapping to particular references.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What conditions or classifications do the revised FAQs impose on this particular investment change?","What existing approval rule governs a change excluded from relief, and does it require prior approval in the specific case?","Does the transition preserve only processing of the pending application, or also prevent withdrawal and use of the new relief for the same change?","When is pending status assessed, and what date governs a change planned before but implemented after 28 November 2025?","How do the relevant home requirements and SFC guidance classify materiality, product novelty or complexity, and possible local policy implications?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["This is a proposal for the circular's stated relief conditions, subject to the unavailable FAQs; it is not a determination of legal correctness.","The specific effective date governs the general immediate-effect wording.","A qualifying application received before the Effective Date and still unapproved at that date stays within the existing process for the selected application.","The exception is disjunctive: novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications independently defeats relief.","Home-supervision language explains the measures; no separate supervision condition is added to item (ii) beyond its express home-requirements condition."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will 